    <section class="cv-summary">
      <h2>Professional Summary</h2>
      <p>I'm a Staff AI Engineer at Contabilizei and the RAG question that keeps breaking hangs on two entities that never appear in the same paragraph. Vector search did its job. It returned the closest chunk.</p>
      <p>Fifteen years in software, five in AI. Here, generative AI in sales and onboarding lifted conversion more than 70%, and support runs on AI agents with LangGraph and Google ADK on Vertex AI. MCP, the Model Context Protocol, came in because I was rewriting an integration for every tool.</p>
      <p>RAG covers the answer that sits in a document. When it sits in the relationship between entities, I reach for GraphRAG: Cypher on Neo4j over an ontology I drew by hand. Nothing ships without evals. LLM-as-Judge, versioned next to the code. LoRA fine-tuning only after prompting and retrieval run dry. Python daily, Golang when latency hurts. GCP now, AWS since 2017.</p>
      <p>Before this, Head of AI at BrandLovrs, creator economy, owning AI strategy and 6 projects. I put a knowledge graph under brand and creator matching. User satisfaction climbed 40%. At XP Inc. I built the first internal chatbot, IBM Watson on serverless AWS Lambda, wired into WhatsApp and Alexa. Human-handled requests fell 25%.</p>
      <p>Five of us spent 48 hours on a detector for oil slicks at sea. It won the global NASA Space Apps prize. The work I like best is forward deployed: sitting with the customer, putting the agent inside their process. That was Hooman, my company, chatbots inside Itaú, Renault and Correios.</p>
    </section>

